{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>Who shall assign it to you as inheritance.</b> For your sake; each and every prince is an apotropos for his tribe, distributing the tribal inheritance to the families and to the men, selecting for each and every one a fitting portion — and what they do is considered done as though you yourselves had done it. And it is not tenable to interpret this <b>לכם</b> like every ״לכם״ in Scripture, for if so it should have written יַנְחִילוּ לָכֶם; יִנְחֲלוּ means that they inherit for you — for your sake and in your place, as in ״HaShem will fight for you״ (Exodus 14)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:13:50.447480774Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}